«Мысленный эксперимент» · высота небоскрёбов · клип карты (map.mp4, film 20.60–30.90 s)
Style: Lemo-Opuscar «3D Map Explainer» (engine copied from styles/map-explainer/demo and adapted). Third-party data and sources:

## Map data and imagery (downloaded by tools/fetch_wide.py and tools/fetch_patch.py into raw/, processed into assets/)
- Imagery: Sentinel-2 cloudless 2016 - https://s2maps.eu by EOX IT Services GmbH (Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data
  2016 & 2017), CC BY 4.0. Layer s2cloudless_3857: zoom 9 for the whole region (Red Sea → Gulf of Oman, 35.5–60.0 E,
  19.0–31.6 N), zoom 11 for two detail patches: Dubai (54.3–56.3 E, 24.2–25.9 N) and Jeddah (38.1–40.1 E, 20.9–22.6 N).
  Only the 2016 release is used (later Sentinel-2 cloudless releases are CC BY-NC-SA). Imagery colour-graded (warmed, sea
  shaded by depth) — "modified".
- Elevation and bathymetry: AWS Terrain Tiles (Mapzen / Tilezen "terrarium" PNG), https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/
  zoom 8 (region) and zoom 10 (the two patches). Sources include SRTM (public domain), GMTED, ETOPO1 and GEBCO; attribution
  as required by the terrain-tiles documentation. Land heights exaggerated ×3.2 (stated on screen: «рельеф ×3,2»).
- Every download URL and date is logged in raw/manifest.jsonl (downloaded 2026-11-27).
- Tower positions: public coordinates — Burj Khalifa 25.1972 N, 55.2744 E; Jeddah Tower 21.7347 N, 39.0858 E.
  Pillars are data graphics, not models of the towers: one slab = 100 m (stated on screen).

